conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bowling ball ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "A heavy, round ball with three holes for fingers. ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I forgot how heavy these bowling balls were!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you to talk about free time activities.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "muscle mass", "type": "name"}, {"content": " the amount of muscle you have on your body", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: I've been gaining muscle mass.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to bowl ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " the action of throwing a ball along a lane in order to knock over pins ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've totally forgotten how to bowl.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "specialized ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "involving specific knowledge or training ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've been going to a specialized cooking class.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "clean eating", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the idea of eating whole or \u201creal\u201d foods, those have not been processed ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The trend of clean eating is something for me to consider.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to tap into", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to gain access to", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: I want to tap into this new market.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "market", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in business, an area or industry", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The clean eating market is getting larger.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "savvy ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "experienced and knowledgeable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That's a very savvy idea!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob02aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Present Perfect Continuous vs Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The Present Perfect tense and the Present Perfect Continuous tense each have their own uses. You use both to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Look at the chart for an outline of the two tenses: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " I've been going to specialized cooking classes for two weeks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Since you started as the manager, you've become attuned to the business side of the restaurant industry.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning/Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject + has/have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to talk about experience\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Since</span> you started as the manager, you've become attuned to the business side of the restaurant industry.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject + has/have + been v-ing \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to describe: <br> a single activity that lasts a long time OR <br> an action that is repeated over a long period of time  <br> <br> when a long activity has just stopped\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I've been going to specialized cooking classes <span class=\\\"strong\\\">for</span> two weeks.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "To emphasize the <span class=\"strong\">action</span>, use the <span class=\"underline\">continuous</span> form. <br> <span class=\"italic\"> <li> They've been studying hard. </li></span></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To emphasize the <span class=\"strong\">result of the action</span>, use the <span class=\"underline\">simple</span> form. <br> <span class=\"italic\"> <li> I've won many cooking awards.</li></span></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li> You use FOR to talk about how long an action has been happening (a week, 2 days, five hours, two weeks, etc.).</li> \t<li>You use SINCE to talk about when the action started (2010, Tuesday, I started,etc.).</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Have you bee